<div class="card">
  <h2>B &middot; Filtering a fetched loop &mdash; two silent traps</h2>
  <table>
  <tr><th>expression</th><th>result</th></tr>
  <tr data-run="&#123;&#123;each &#123;this.integration_test&#125;.json(programs) as p&#125;&#125;&#123;&#123;if &#123;p.parent&#125; == 'cat-sports'&#125;&#125;&lt;b&gt;&#123;&#123;!p.title&#125;&#125;&lt;/b&gt; &#123;&#123;end-if&#125;&#125;&#123;&#123;end-each&#125;&#125;"><td><code>&#123;&#123;if &#123;p.parent&#125; == 'cat-sports'&#125;&#125;</code><br><span class="why">inner if, value QUOTED</span></td><td style="background:#e7f5ee">&#9989; {{each {this.integration_test}.json(programs) as p}}{{if {p.parent} == 'cat-sports'}}<b>{{!p.title}}</b> {{end-if}}{{end-each}}&mdash; correctly filtered, 2 of 3</td></tr>
  <tr data-run="&#123;&#123;each &#123;this.integration_test&#125;.json(programs) as p&#125;&#125;&#123;&#123;if &#123;p.parent&#125; == (cat-sports)&#125;&#125;&lt;b&gt;&#123;&#123;!p.title&#125;&#125;&lt;/b&gt; &#123;&#123;end-if&#125;&#125;&#123;&#123;end-each&#125;&#125;"><td><code>&#123;&#123;if &#123;p.parent&#125; == (cat-sports)&#125;&#125;</code><br><span class="why">same value, PARENTHESES &mdash; note the hyphen</span></td><td style="background:#fdeaea">&#128680; {{each {this.integration_test}.json(programs) as p}}{{if {p.parent} == (cat-sports)}}<b>{{!p.title}}</b> {{end-if}}{{end-each}}<br><b>matches EVERYTHING</b> &mdash; the hyphen breaks the parens form</td></tr>
  <tr data-run="&#123;&#123;each &#123;this.integration_test&#125;.json(programs) as p where p.parent == 'cat-sports'&#125;&#125;&lt;b&gt;&#123;&#123;!p.title&#125;&#125;&lt;/b&gt; &#123;&#123;end-each&#125;&#125;"><td><code>&#123;&#123;each &#8230; as p where p.parent == 'cat-sports'&#125;&#125;</code></td><td style="background:#fff6e0">&#9888; {{each {this.integration_test}.json(programs) as p where p.parent == 'cat-sports'}}<b>{{!p.title}}</b> {{end-each}}<br><b>where is IGNORED</b> &mdash; every row, including cat-aquatics</td></tr>
  </table>
  <div class="note" style="border-left-color:var(--bad);background:#fffafa"><b style="color:var(--bad)">The hyphen trap.</b> A value containing <code>-</code> inside parentheses is not compared &mdash; it matches every row. Quote it instead. This matters because <b>Zesty ZUIDs contain hyphens</b> (<code>7-feeac0fae9-28d0cs</code>) while <b>Salesforce ids do not</b> (<code>a31a6000000EhmvAAC</code>), so the parens form is safe for Traction Rec ids and unsafe for ZUIDs. Part&nbsp;1&nbsp;&sect;2 compares a Salesforce id, which is why it is correct.</div>
  <div class="note"><b>Two more of the same family.</b> <code>limit</code> is ignored on a fetched loop just like <code>where</code>. And <code>FIND_IN_SET</code> inside an <code>if</code> on fetched JSON is <b>always true</b> &mdash; it returns every row while looking like a filter. On a <i>content model</i> the same function evaluates correctly. Same spelling, opposite behaviour.<br><br>Also: in a <code>where</code> clause use a <b>single</b> <code>=</code>; the doubled <code>==</code> matches nothing, silently.</div>
</div>

