  <tr><th>expression</th><th>result</th></tr>
  <tr data-run="&#123;&#123;each api.json.get(https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com/users) as u&#125;&#125;&#123;&#123;!u.name&#125;&#125;; &#123;&#123;end-each&#125;&#125;"><td><code>api.json.get(https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com/users)</code><br><span class="why">EXTERNAL domain</span></td><td style="background:#e7f5ee">&#9989; {{each api.json.get(https://jsonplaceholder.typicode.com/users) as u}}{{!u.name}}; {{end-each}}</td></tr>
  </table>
</div>

<div class="card">
  <h2>E &middot; Why the proxy service is still required</h2>
  <p class="why">Parsley can reach the internet &mdash; but not Traction Rec:</p>
  <ul style="margin:0 0 4px;padding-left:20px;color:#333;font-size:14px">
    <li><code>api.json.get(url)</code> sends <b>no headers</b>, and TR returns 401 for <code>?access_token=</code> in the query string (verified).</li>
    <li>Minting a token is a <b>POST</b>; this is GET-only.</li>
    <li>A Zesty view is a <b>public URL</b>, so the client secret could never live in one.</li>
  </ul>
  <p style="margin:10px 0 0;font-size:14px">The conclusion survives; the reason recorded for it was wrong.</p>
</div>

